hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"73","Abu Hurayrah also reported that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ﷺ recited in the two rakʿahs before fajr prayer: Qul yā ayyuhal kāfiroon and Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad. Reference: Sunan an-Nasa'i 945 ."
"74","Jābir reported: “During the two rakʿahs of ṭawāf, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ﷺ recited the two suwar: Qul yā ayyuhal kāfirūn (Sūrat al-Kāfirūn), and Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad (Sūrat al-Ikhlāṣ).” Reference: Jami` at-Tirmidhi 869 ."
"75","Ubayy reported: \In the first rakʿah of witr (prayer)"","" the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ﷺ used to recite: “Sabbiḥ isma rabbikal-aʿlā (Sūrat al-Aʿlā)"","" in the second"","" Qul yā ayyuhal kāfirūn (Sūrat al-Kāfirūn)"","" and in the third (rakʿah)"","" Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad (Sūrat al-Ikhlāṣ).” Reference: Sunan an-Nasa'i 1699 ."""""
